<%- include('partials/head', { title: title, robots: locals.robots }) %>
<% if (!viewerIsPublic) { %><%- include('partials/spine', { nav: 'seasons' }) %><% } %>

<main class="sheet" data-key="seasons">
  <span class="crop tl" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="crop tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop bl" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="crop br" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <div class="block pt-20" id="block">

    <%- include('partials/desk', { deskQuery: '' }) %>

    <%#
      §7 — the lookbook, in order, one continuous scroll.

      Nothing here has a progress bar or a completion percentage, and there
      is no target anywhere in the feature. The subject is how time passed,
      not how much was accomplished.
    %>

    <%# ── 1. FRONT MATTER ────────────────────────────── %>
    <div class="eyebrow mono">
      <span class="tag">SEASON</span>
      <span class="dim">
        <%= meta.short %><%
          if (row.state === 'closed' && row.closed_at) { %> · CLOSED <%= h.monthDay(row.closed_at) %><%
          } %>
      </span>
      <%# §9 — the OPEN marker is the only red in the feature. %>
      <% if (row.state === 'open') { %><span class="season-open mono-s">OPEN</span><% } %>
    </div>

    <h1 class="season-title"><%= row.given_title || meta.label %></h1>

    <% if (strip.length) { %>
      <%# One band per book, in finish order — the colour each book was
          derived to carry, or the one its reader chose instead. A book with
          no evidence gets no colour: it is drawn as a hatch, which is a
          state and not a gap. §05.

          The emotion words are in the label rather than on the bands: at
          this height there is no room for type, and colour on its own
          carries no meaning to anyone who cannot see it. %>
      <div class="season-strip" role="img" aria-label="<%= h.stripLabel(strip) %>">
        <% strip.forEach(function(b) { %>
          <i class="<%= h.bandClass(b) %>"<% if (b.hex) { %> id="<%= h.rule(styleRules, 'sb', b.hex, 'background:' + h.css.color(b.hex)) %>"<% } %>></i>
        <% }) %>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <%# ── 2. THE NOTE ────────────────────────────────── %>
    <%# §3 — an open season has no note. "You cannot review a collection
        mid-show." §12 — a season under three books has none either. %>
    <% if (row.note) { %>
      <p class="season-note"><%= row.note %></p>

      <%#
        The jump-links that used to sit here — EDIT, REGENERATE,
        REGENERATED TODAY, COMPOSED FROM THE FACTS — pointed at controls
        that are already visible further down this page, under their own
        headings. A row of anchors duplicating what is on screen is a table
        of contents for a page you can see all of.

        The lookbook stays: it is a different object, and this is the only
        way to it.
      %>
      <%#
        THE TWO OBJECTS, AS CONTROLS.

        These were two 11px grey links separated by a middot, at the foot of
        a block of statistics — the same treatment as a field label, for the
        only two things on this page anybody actually goes to. The lookbook
        and the poster are what a season is FOR; the page above them is the
        record they are made from.

        So they take the treatment the publish button used to have. The
        lookbook is filled, because it is the object; the poster carries the
        same weight in outline, because it is one press of the same season.
        Two controls on a page whose entire purpose is to lead to them is
        not a breach of "one accent per screen" — it is the screen.
      %>
      <% if (isOwner && !viewerIsPublic) { %>
        <p class="season-controls">
          <a class="btn-do" href="/season/<%= row.code %>/lookbook">THE LOOKBOOK</a>
          <a class="btn-do" href="/season/<%= row.code %>/poster.png">THE POSTER</a>
        </p>

        <%#
          ── PUBLISHING ────────────────────────────────

          The lookbook and the poster are the best objects this product makes
          and both were sealed inside an account that defaults to private.

          The way out is NOT "make your profile public". It is publishing one
          artifact, once: a closed season, at whatever visibility the account
          keeps. Scoped, reversible, and legible — which is what lets
          private-by-default survive a product that also wants to be shared.
        %>
        <%# PUBLISHING IS GONE.

            A season could be published as one link anyone could open. The
            argument for it was that the lookbook and the poster are the most
            shareable things this product makes and they were sealed inside a
            private account. That was true and it was still the wrong answer:
            a season is a record of what one person read and thought about
            it, the marginalia in it is their own writing, and handing that a
            public URL made a personal object into something to be
            circulated. If a reader wants to show somebody, they can show
            them. The product does not need to mint a link for it. %>
      <% } %>
    <% } %>

    <% if (locals.error) { %><p class="field-error mono-s"><%= error %></p><% } %>

    <%# ── 3. MOVEMENTS AND FRAMES ────────────────────── %>
    <% movements.forEach(function(m) { %>
      <section class="movement <%= m.is_empty ? 'movement-empty' : '' %>">
        <div class="movement-head">
          <h2 class="movement-name">
            <span class="movement-numeral"><%= m.roman %>.</span> <%= m.name %>
          </h2>
          <div class="movement-meta mono-s">
            <%= h.monthDay(m.starts_on) %> · <%= h.monthDay(m.ends_on) %>
            · <%= m.is_empty ? 'NOTHING' : m.books.length + (m.books.length === 1 ? ' BOOK' : ' BOOKS') %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%#
          §6 — the empty movement. A name, a date range, a count of zero,
          and nothing beneath it but a hairline.

          No commentary. No prompt to read more. Not collapsed. A month in
          which somebody did not read is part of their season.
        %>
        <% if (!m.is_empty) { %>
          <div class="frames">
            <% m.books.forEach(function(f) { %>
              <%- include('partials/frame', { f: f, isOwner: isOwner, viewerIsPublic: viewerIsPublic, code: row.code }) %>
            <% }) %>
          </div>
        <% } %>
      </section>
    <% }) %>

    <%# Frames with no movement: an open season, or one with no structure. %>
    <% if (loose.length) { %>
      <div class="frames <%= movements.length ? 'mt-34' : '' %>">
        <% loose.forEach(function(f) { %>
          <%- include('partials/frame', { f: f, isOwner: isOwner, viewerIsPublic: viewerIsPublic, code: row.code }) %>
        <% }) %>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <%# §12 — a season with nothing in it shows the date range and nothing
        else. No message, no prompt, no encouragement. %>
    <% if (!frames.length) { %>
      <p class="season-range mono-s dim">
        <%= h.monthDay(meta.starts_on) %> · <%= h.monthDay(meta.ends_on) %>
      </p>
    <% } %>

    <%# ── 5. ABSENCES ────────────────────────────────── %>
    <%# §7.5 — listed plainly. No commentary. %>
    <% if (absences.length) { %>
      <h2 class="sec mt-44">Set down</h2>
      <% absences.forEach(function(a) { %>
        <div class="absence">
          <span class="absence-title"><%= a.title %></span>
          <span class="frame-author"><%= a.author || '' %></span>
          <span class="mono-s dim"><% if (a.page) { %>P.<%= Math.round(a.page) %><% } %></span>
        </div>
      <% }) %>
    <% } %>

    <%# ── 6. THE COLOPHON ────────────────────────────── %>
    <%# §7.6 — the credits page. No charts, no bars, no graphs. %>
    <% if (colophon.length) { %>
      <h2 class="sec mt-44">Colophon</h2>
      <dl class="season-colophon">
        <% colophon.forEach(function(p) { %>
          <div><dt><%= p.label %></dt><dd><%= p.value %></dd></div>
        <% }) %>
      </dl>
    <% } %>

    <%# ── SHARE, and the four editing controls ───────── %>
    <%# §12 — "0 books: Season exists, shows the date range and nothing
        else. No message, no prompt, no encouragement." A poster link and a
        regenerate button are prompts. %>
    <% if (row.state === 'closed' && isOwner && !viewerIsPublic && frames.length) { %>
      <%# POSTER → is gone from here: the poster is a filled control at the
          top of this page, and a second link to it at the foot was the same
          door twice. EDIT THE NOTE and REGENERATE THE ANALYSIS went with it.

          What that costs is stated rather than hidden: a season's note and
          its given title can no longer be edited by hand, and the analysis
          cannot be asked for again. The routes behind both were removed with
          the controls, because a POST nothing can reach is worse than no
          POST at all. `npm run seasons` still closes and writes seasons. %>
      <% if (locals.user && user.profile_visibility === 'public' && user.username) { %>
        <p class="mono-s mt-44">
          <a class="more-link" href="/@<%= user.username %>/<%= row.code %>">PUBLIC PAGE →</a>
        </p>
      <% } %>
    <% } %>

  </div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
